01:14:01.905 --> 01:14:03.628
Tom. the fatter you get.
the sadder you get.

1197
01:14:03.728 --> 01:14:05.671
Will you two stop flirting
for a minute?

1198
01:14:05.771 --> 01:14:09.972
After we pay Hatchet.
this deal puts us up...

1199
01:14:10.384 --> 01:14:13.020
nearly 200.000 pounds each.

1200
01:14:13.766 --> 01:14:18.611
That's not bad for a morning's work.
I think you'll agree.

1201
01:14:27.007 --> 01:14:28.514
So they had the cash.

1202
01:14:28.614 --> 01:14:29.473
And the puff.

1203
01:14:29.573 --> 01:14:32.549
Cheeky bastards. Count it.

1204
01:14:32.669 --> 01:14:34.609
Shit. Dog. There's a lot.

1205
01:14:34.709 --> 01:14:37.344
Do you want to do it next door?

1206
01:14:37.456 --> 01:14:38.423
We're not going next door

1207
01:14:38.523 --> 01:14:41.551
'til we've flayed
them dead men walking.

1208
01:14:41.651 --> 01:14:42.739
We'll count it upstairs.

1209
01:14:42.839 --> 01:14:45.902
I don't want them to see you fingering the
money when they walk through the door...

1210
01:14:46.002 --> 01:14:48.002
Dog. look...

1211
01:14:48.564 --> 01:14:51.832
Give it us here... dozy bastard.

1212
01:14:54.350 --> 01:14:56.776
Check your guns.
Get yourselves well hid.

1213
01:14:56.876 --> 01:15:01.100
You wait till they get right inside
the door. then you give it to'em.

1214
01:15:01.200 --> 01:15:04.855
Give me them shooters.
you can use your own.

1215
01:15:14.580 --> 01:15:15.332
Yeah.

1216
01:15:15.432 --> 01:15:17.218
That's no way
to answer the phone.

1217
01:15:17.318 --> 01:15:18.613
Is that you. Dean?

1218
01:15:18.713 --> 01:15:21.162
No. it's Lord fucking Lucan.
Who do you think it is?

1219
01:15:21.262 --> 01:15:22.590
What can I do for you?

1220
01:15:22.690 --> 01:15:25.367
You know those guns I sold you.
I need them back.

1221
01:15:25.467 --> 01:15:28.225
Not likely I'm afraid. I don't think
I'll be seeing them again.

1222
01:15:28.325 --> 01:15:30.118
Look. I've got the money
to pay for them.

1223
01:15:30.218 --> 01:15:32.746
I'm sure you do.
But don't think you understand.

1224
01:15:32.846 --> 01:15:35.476
I ain't gonna be seeing them
or the guns again.

1225
01:15:35.576 --> 01:15:36.822
We can't get them.

1226
01:15:36.922 --> 01:15:38.848
If we can't get them.
we can't get them.

1227
01:15:38.948 --> 01:15:40.810
Well. you'll have to fucking get them.

1228
01:15:40.910 --> 01:15:43.264
We made a fucking deal for
everything inside the cabinet.

1229
01:15:43.364 --> 01:15:46.496
Inside. out-fucking-side -
I don't give a shit.

1230
01:15:46.596 --> 01:15:48.720
- You get those guns
because if you don't...

1231
01:15:48.820 --> 01:15:49.890
Oh yeah. Bazza. or what?

1232
01:15:49.990 --> 01:15:52.054
Have you heard
of Harry Lonsdale?

1233
01:15:52.154 --> 01:15:55.540
Otherwise known as "Hack You
Up With an Hatchet Harry"?

1234
01:15:55.640 --> 01:15:57.688
Well. this is...

1235
01:15:57.957 --> 01:16:00.545
James Bond. need-to-know time.

1236
01:16:00.674 --> 01:16:04.666
When you dance with the devil.
you wait for the song to stop.

1237
01:16:04.766 --> 01:16:06.766
Know what I mean?

1238
01:16:10.891 --> 01:16:14.158
I mean find 'em.
torture 'em and kill 'em.

1239
01:16:14.258 --> 01:16:16.268
And bring back
what belongs to me.

1240
01:16:16.368 --> 01:16:20.869
Because if you don't.
your family's bang in trouble.

1241
01:16:21.917 --> 01:16:23.397
Who was that?

1242
01:16:23.497 --> 01:16:25.332
That was Harry Horrible Hatchet.

1243
01:16:25.432 --> 01:16:26.842
Jesus. I've heard of him.

1244
01:16:26.942 --> 01:16:30.342
Shit. they were
his fucking guns we sold.

1245
01:16:30.358 --> 01:16:31.960
We've got to find them.

1246
01:16:32.060 --> 01:16:37.075
Now no fucking about now. Nick.
Where can I find those guns?

1247
01:17:07.442 --> 01:17:09.313
Six black cocks
and a little white kitten

1248
01:17:09.413 --> 01:17:12.048
sitting on the side
of the road.

1249
01:17:14.090 --> 01:17:17.122
We're gonna do
a proper decoration job.

1250
01:17:17.222 --> 01:17:20.581
I want the grey skies
of London illuminated.

1251
01:17:20.681 --> 01:17:23.231
I want that house painted red.

1252
01:17:24.974 --> 01:17:28.058
All right. there's this brass
standing on the corner. right?

1253
01:17:28.158 --> 01:17:30.825
Dwarf walks up to her
carrying a suitcase...

1254
01:17:30.925 --> 01:17:32.787
Winston there
is gonna come along

1255
01:17:32.887 --> 01:17:35.360
and see if he recognises
any of them.

1256
01:17:35.460 --> 01:17:37.940
Now watch out for these fellas -

1257
01:17:38.040 --> 01:17:42.131
they've got a bit of an arsenal
and they don't mind using it.

1258
01:17:42.231 --> 01:17:45.376
...and I'm taking down her panties...

1259
01:17:46.348 --> 01:17:48.858
Now does everyone here know
what they got to do?

1260
01:17:48.958 --> 01:17:50.958
Yeah.

1261
01:18:57.612 --> 01:18:59.822
What the fuck is going on?

1262
01:19:41.576 --> 01:19:44.891
You got something here
for me. have you?

1263
01:19:45.263 --> 01:19:47.777
Come on. chop-chop.

1264
01:19:54.591 --> 01:19:56.591
Thank you very much.

1265
01:19:57.602 --> 01:19:59.485
- He's got the guns.
Go ahead you get them.

1266
01:19:59.585 --> 01:20:00.823
Why me?

1267
01:20:00.923 --> 01:20:02.900
You're supposed
to be the hard case...

1268
01:20:03.000 --> 01:20:06.060
You go get the guns!
I drive the car!

1269
01:20:10.350 --> 01:20:11.190
Good boy.

1270
01:20:11.290 --> 01:20:12.548
- Go get the fucking guns.

1271
01:20:12.648 --> 01:20:15.601
I'm not going get the fucking
guns! YOU get the fucking guns!

1272
01:20:15.701 --> 01:20:17.701
You fucking big...

1273
01:20:20.891 --> 01:20:22.528
All right. Wrap them guns up.

1274
01:20:22.628 --> 01:20:24.628
Count the money.

1275
01:20:24.728 --> 01:20:26.268
Put your seat belt on.

1276
01:20:26.368 --> 01:20:31.553
Fucking guns. we've got to get the fucking
guns or we're dead!

1277
01:20:44.422 --> 01:20:48.842
.. so I made sure I fucked
the one that was coughing.

1278
01:21:00.422 --> 01:21:04.250
Out of the car. you yuppy fucker!
Aaaaaaaagh!

1279
01:21:31.145 --> 01:21:32.698
He's the one
we shot in the neck.

1280
01:21:32.798 --> 01:21:35.665
Is that right. Mr Botanical?

1281
01:22:00.648 --> 01:22:02.772
Jesus!

1282
01:22:14.430 --> 01:22:17.762
I don't believe this.
What the fuck has happened here?

1283
01:22:17.862 --> 01:22:19.862
Jesus.

1284
01:22:20.944 --> 01:22:23.950
The money. The gear.

1285
01:22:34.901 --> 01:22:36.639
This is fucked.

1286
01:22:36.739 --> 01:22:39.232
No money. No weed.

1287
01:22:40.040 --> 01:22:42.959
It's all been replaced
by a pile of corpses.

1288
01:22:43.059 --> 01:22:46.235
All right. Don't panic.
Let's think about this.

1289
01:22:46.335 --> 01:22:49.083
No. fuck that.
you can think about it.

1290
01:22:49.183 --> 01:22:51.754
I'm panicking and I'm off.

1291
01:22:59.513 --> 01:23:01.405
How did you get your hands
on these. then?

1292
01:23:01.505 --> 01:23:02.751
The boys had 'em.

1293
01:23:02.851 --> 01:23:04.012
I know you like
these sort of things -

1294
01:23:04.112 --> 01:23:06.174
wondered if you wanted 'em.

1295
01:23:06.274 --> 01:23:08.314
Yeah. I'll have 'em.

1296
01:23:08.474 --> 01:23:12.639
- Was it hard getting the money?
- Not especially.

1297
01:23:12.954 --> 01:23:15.589
Upset a few characters. though.

1298
01:23:16.426 --> 01:23:17.540
Have you counted it?

1299
01:23:17.640 --> 01:23:19.519
Yeah. it's all there.
to the pound.

1300
01:23:19.619 --> 01:23:21.760
- And they were gonna pay?
- Looks like it.

1301
01:23:21.860 --> 01:23:24.609
But who knows?
The opportunity was there.

1302
01:23:24.709 --> 01:23:27.693
In my experience it's best
to take that opportunity -

1303
01:23:27.793 --> 01:23:29.793
if it's there.

1304
01:23:30.195 --> 01:23:32.195
Good work. Chris.

1305
01:23:38.877 --> 01:23:40.332
We've got to get those guns.

1306
01:23:40.432 --> 01:23:42.887
This is dangerous shit there.
We don't even know who lives there.

1307
01:23:42.987 --> 01:23:44.792
Listen. I don't care who lives there!

1308
01:23:44.892 --> 01:23:48.328
All's I know is that it's preferable
to death by Hatchet.

1309
01:23:48.428 --> 01:23:51.278
Fair enough. Let's go.

1310
01:24:13.775 --> 01:24:16.395
I don't think
it's the right move.

1311
01:24:16.495 --> 01:24:17.506
It's either that

1312
01:24:17.606 --> 01:24:21.431
the old boy's place
and we lose a digit daily.

1313
01:24:21.680 --> 01:24:24.285
- I'm gonna phone him.
- As if he'll care.

1314
01:24:24.385 --> 01:24:27.348
He'll care. all right? That was
supposed to be his money.

1315
01:24:27.448 --> 01:24:29.509
Whether he cares about us
or not. is different.

1316
01:24:29.609 --> 01:24:31.609
Pass me the phone.

1317
01:24:46.428 --> 01:24:49.114
Yeah? That you. boy?

1318
01:24:49.210 --> 01:24:51.456
It's Ed.
if that's what you mean.

1319
01:24:51.556 --> 01:24:53.554
'Pay day. ain't it?'

1320
01:24:53.564 --> 01:24:56.746
Yeah... I wanted
to talk to you about that.

1321
01:24:56.846 --> 01:24:58.587
I'll bet you do.

1322
01:24:58.687 --> 01:25:00.485
I got half
a million nicker sitting here.

1323
01:25:00.585 --> 01:25:02.859
which means
some poor sod doesn't.

1324
01:25:02.959 --> 01:25:06.274
You've been upsetin' a few people. boy.

1325
01:25:06.498 --> 01:25:09.008
But that really
isn't my concern. is it?

1326
01:25:09.108 --> 01:25:12.763
What does concern me...
is the guns you had.

1327
01:25:12.966 --> 01:25:15.115
'I want to talk to you
about that.'

1328
01:25:15.215 --> 01:25:19.380
So get your arse over here now.
And I do mean now!

1329
01:25:52.438 --> 01:25:57.042
Bastard! You fucking bastard!

1330
01:26:05.537 --> 01:26:08.257
What the fuck
are you doing here?

1331
01:26:09.201 --> 01:26:13.009
What the fuck
are you doing here?

1332
01:26:23.454 --> 01:26:27.132
Job well done. We made
a few quid out of that one.

1333
01:26:27.232 --> 01:26:27.987
Son...?

1334
01:26:28.087 --> 01:26:30.212
Made a few quid. did you?

1335
01:26:30.492 --> 01:26:32.617
Where's what I want. now?

1336
01:26:33.590 --> 01:26:34.822
You all right down there. mate?

1337
01:26:34.922 --> 01:26:38.237
Very fucking funny.
Where's what I want?

1338
01:26:38.713 --> 01:26:40.394
I've just left it in the office.

1339
01:26:40.494 --> 01:26:42.416
Well. we'd better go to
the office and get it.

1340
01:26:42.516 --> 01:26:44.921
that is if you want
your son to see his next birthday.

1341
01:26:45.021 --> 01:26:49.186
- Now chop-fucking-chop.
- All right. Fair enough.

1342
01:26:50.198 --> 01:26:52.198
Where you going?

1343
01:26:52.294 --> 01:26:55.393
It's a thirty second drive
or a five minute walk.

1344
01:26:55.493 --> 01:26:59.998
I couldn't have parked outside.
I'd have got a ticket.

1345
01:27:00.232 --> 01:27:01.633
I suppose that don't
matter now. does it?

1346
01:27:01.733 --> 01:27:03.733
Just be careful.

1347
01:27:03.774 --> 01:27:05.774
Right.

1348
01:27:12.076 --> 01:27:13.195
You and me.

1349
01:27:13.295 --> 01:27:14.087
You and who?

1350
01:27:14.187 --> 01:27:17.417
You know where
the door handle is. Tom.

1351
01:27:19.148 --> 01:27:22.578
# "The Payback" #
by James Brown

1352
01:27:23.591 --> 01:27:25.591
# Pay back

1353
01:27:25.727 --> 01:27:29.136
# That's it. pay back.

1354
01:27:30.252 --> 01:27:32.777
# Revenge. I'm mad

1355
01:27:33.987 --> 01:27:36.452
# Get down with my girlfriend

1356
01:27:37.619 --> 01:27:38.790
# That ain't right ##

1357
01:27:38.890 --> 01:27:41.138
Oh. no. Not again.

1358
01:27:56.339 --> 01:27:58.579
That's it. I'm off.

1359
01:27:59.319 --> 01:28:03.220
Tom... that is our bag.

1360
01:28:20.660 --> 01:28:23.301
- Ed...!
- Hold on.

1361
01:28:34.963 --> 01:28:37.161
This is our bag.

1362
01:28:39.532 --> 01:28:40.624
That's it. We're off.

1363
01:28:40.724 --> 01:28:42.686
- I'll see you in the car.
I'm gonna take these guns.

1364
01:28:42.786 --> 01:28:43.504
Tom. don't fuck about!

1365
01:28:43.604 --> 01:28:48.704
- I'll see you in the car. -
Tom! - It'll only take a minute.

1366
01:29:01.546 --> 01:29:03.234
What is going on?

1367
01:29:03.334 --> 01:29:08.285
I don't know. but what I do know
is there's no more Harry.

1368
01:29:08.769 --> 01:29:10.968
Which means
there's no more debt.

1369
01:29:11.068 --> 01:29:14.645
And if there's no more debt.
there's no more problem.

1370
01:29:14.745 --> 01:29:18.285
And there's no problem with the
neighbours - because they're all dead.

1371
01:29:18.385 --> 01:29:21.560
And I think.
if I get this right.

1372
01:29:22.187 --> 01:29:26.692
we haven't done anything wrong
and we're in the clear.

1373
01:29:57.370 --> 01:29:59.267
Never ever...

1374
01:29:59.367 --> 01:30:03.452
has anyone
been as fucking rude...

1375
01:30:03.850 --> 01:30:05.448
.. to me...

1376
01:30:05.548 --> 01:30:10.470
...as you. YOU... FUCKING... BASTARD!

1377
01:30:26.972 --> 01:30:28.972
You all right. mate?

1378
01:30:29.392 --> 01:30:31.952
Cheeky bastard!

1379
01:30:48.738 --> 01:30:51.654
'Now this was an embarrassing
position for Tom to be in.

1380
01:30:51.754 --> 01:30:54.260
'But Chris had to respect
the fact that he was holding

1381
01:30:54.360 --> 01:30:57.212
'what appeared to be
a pair of loaded shotguns.

1382
01:30:57.312 --> 01:31:00.691
'And Tom had to respect the fact
that they were not loaded.

1383
01:31:00.791 --> 01:31:03.893
'So without anybody
losing too much face.

1384
01:31:03.993 --> 01:31:07.585
'Tom left through a side door
and Chris left with the money.

1385
01:31:07.685 --> 01:31:10.575
'And everybody else got arrested.'

1386
01:31:13.995 --> 01:31:15.995
He's not one of 'em.

1387
01:31:18.956 --> 01:31:23.317
# Sitting in the cheap seats
underneath the stars

1388
01:31:24.947 --> 01:31:27.196
# I'm heading back to base

1389
01:31:27.389 --> 01:31:29.854
# I'll drop you off
at mars ##

1390
01:31:30.109 --> 01:31:34.104
I think your dad would like
a word with you. Ed.

1391
01:31:36.641 --> 01:31:37.822
Where are the others?

1392
01:31:37.922 --> 01:31:41.917
They got out yesterday.
They're back at the bar.

1393
01:31:44.836 --> 01:31:46.836
# I'm a man machine

1394
01:31:47.869 --> 01:31:49.869
# Takin' gasoline

1395
01:31:51.198 --> 01:31:53.791
# Super-human being ##

1396
01:31:55.657 --> 01:31:56.855
All right. Dad?

1397
01:31:56.955 --> 01:31:59.459
I'm all right.
How about yourself?

1398
01:31:59.559 --> 01:32:03.600
I'm all right.
Could do with a drink. though.

1399
01:32:03.983 --> 01:32:06.856
All in good time. All in good time.

1400
01:32:06.956 --> 01:32:09.728
So. are you in the clear?

1401
01:32:09.920 --> 01:32:12.519
More importantly... am I?

1402
01:32:13.745 --> 01:32:15.745
It appears so.

1403
01:32:15.905 --> 01:32:20.766
Appears? You'll have to do
better than fucking appears. my friend.

1404
01:32:20.866 --> 01:32:22.226
Well. everybody's dead. Dad.

1405
01:32:22.326 --> 01:32:25.622
I think that's about as clear
as it can get.

1406
01:32:25.722 --> 01:32:27.200
How about that drink?

1407
01:32:27.300 --> 01:32:28.876
You know where the bar is.

1408
01:32:28.976 --> 01:32:30.976
Eh?

1409
01:32:31.570 --> 01:32:33.218
Don't make yourself
too comfortable.

1410
01:32:33.318 --> 01:32:36.083
Alan's got to sit there.
Alan!

1411
01:32:39.042 --> 01:32:41.118
You're lucky
you're still breathing.

1412
01:32:41.218 --> 01:32:43.218
let alone able to walk.

1413
01:32:43.506 --> 01:32:47.416
I suggest you take
full advantage of that fact.

1414
01:32:53.511 --> 01:32:56.836
# 'Cause I'm a man machine

1415
01:32:57.617 --> 01:32:59.679
# Takin' gasoline

1416
01:33:00.596 --> 01:33:02.596
# I'm a teen dream

1417
01:33:02.834 --> 01:33:04.665
# Super-human being

1418
01:33:04.765 --> 01:33:07.325
# I'm a man machine

1419
01:33:07.405 --> 01:33:10.486
# I'm a man machine! ##

1420
01:33:10.605 --> 01:33:14.261
You took your time.
Where the hell have you been?

1421
01:33:14.361 --> 01:33:16.401
Sit down. I'll tell you.

1422
01:33:21.683 --> 01:33:25.988
The traffic warden identified
the neighbours' bodies.

1423
01:33:26.088 --> 01:33:28.978
Which sort of
puts us in the clear.

1424
01:33:29.047 --> 01:33:31.997
The only thing connecting us
with the case...

1425
01:33:32.097 --> 01:33:33.648
.. is those shotguns.

1426
01:33:33.748 --> 01:33:35.958
And Tom took care of them.

1427
01:33:36.952 --> 01:33:41.202
You did take care of the shotguns.
didn't you. Tom?

1428
01:33:41.692 --> 01:33:43.337
I wanted to talk to you about that.

1429
01:33:43.437 --> 01:33:45.437
Well. talk.

1430
01:33:45.723 --> 01:33:48.729
Well. actually... no.

1431
01:33:50.265 --> 01:33:51.153
I've got them sittin' in the car.

1432
01:33:51.253 --> 01:33:52.564
I.. I was gonna sell 'em
back to Nick the Greek.

1433
01:33:52.664 --> 01:33:54.860
but I am having a bit of a problem
gettin' hold of him.

1434
01:33:54.960 --> 01:33:56.297
You dippy bastard.

1435
01:33:56.397 --> 01:34:02.183
So... the only thing
connecting us with the case

1436
01:34:02.480 --> 01:34:05.361
is in the back of your car.
which is parked outside!

1437
01:34:05.461 --> 01:34:09.711
They costed 700 quid.
I'm not gonna throw 'em away.

1438
01:34:09.810 --> 01:34:12.701
And they're hardly likely to trace
'em back to us. are they?

